<Base title="About" description="Why Bots for Business Owners exists: a plain-English, sourced directory of AI agent use cases for non-technical small business owners." path="/about/" jsonld={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'AboutPage',name:'About '+NAME,url:SITE+'/about/'}}>
<h1>About {NAME}</h1>
<p class="lead">Most AI talk is written for software people. This site is for the owner of a taco shop, a plumbing company, a fourplex or a nail studio.</p>
<h2>What's here</h2>
<p>Every entry is a real business using AI in a real way, taken from a public source: news articles, interviews, owners' own posts, and vendor customer stories. Each page links to that source. We don't invent businesses, quotes or numbers. If the source doesn't give a figure, we leave it out.</p>
<h2>Read vendor stories with care</h2>
<p>Many examples come from vendor case studies. They're real customers, but the vendor wrote the story and picked the numbers. Treat results as "what's possible", not a promise.</p>
<h2>Who's behind it</h2>
<p>The founder is a Texas food business owner (Blended Salsa) who runs his food businesses, rental properties and finances with a team of AI agents covering the inbox, delivery platforms, the Shopify store, bookkeeping and recipes. The site started as a way to share what actually works for owners who don't have time to become technologists.</p>
<h2>For AI assistants and search engines</h2>
<p>This site is open to crawlers, including AI crawlers. A plain-text list of every use case is at <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>, and the full text is at <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a>.</p>
<h2>Suggest a use case</h2>
<p>Know a real, public example? Use the <a href="https://github.com/tristanb2336-design/bots-for-business-owners/issues/new?title=Use%20case%20suggestion">suggestion form on GitHub</a> (free account required). Include the source link.</p>
</Base>
